.Trashes

# ── Xcode / Swift ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.xcodeproj/
*.xcworkspace/
!*.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
build/
.build/
*.xcuserstate
*.xcscmblueprint
*.hmap
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip
*.dSYM
Package.resolved.bak
apps/ios/StoryArc.xcodeproj/

# …except the app target's resolved dependency graph. The rest of the project is
# regenerated by xcodegen and worthless in review, but this one file is the only
# record of which revision of each Swift package the shipped binary was built
# from. Without it a fresh checkout re-resolves every `from:` edge to whatever is
# newest and nobody sees a diff. Re-including it means re-including each parent
# first: git will not look inside a directory it has already excluded.
!apps/ios/StoryArc.xcodeproj/
apps/ios/StoryArc.xcodeproj/*
!apps/ios/StoryArc.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/
apps/ios/StoryArc.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/*
!apps/ios/StoryArc.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/
apps/ios/StoryArc.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/*
!apps/ios/StoryArc.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/
apps/ios/StoryArc.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/*
!apps/ios/StoryArc.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/Package.resolved

